.SH NAME
hed\-session \- Saves and restores the list of open buffers for the
current cwd.
Used by the reload plugin to survive :reload, and exposed directly so
you can take ad\-hoc workspace snapshots.
.PP
Saves and restores the list of open buffers for the current cwd.
Used by the \f[CR]reload\f[R] plugin to survive \f[CR]:reload\f[R], and
exposed directly so you can take ad\-hoc workspace snapshots.
.SH Commands
.IP
.EX
:session\-save        # write open buffers to the cache file
:session\-restore     # restore from the cache file
.EE
.PP
The cache file lives at
\f[CR]\[ti]/.cache/hed/<encoded\-cwd>/session\f[R].
The cwd is encoded by replacing \f[CR]/\f[R] with \f[CR]%\f[R], so each
working directory gets its own session.
.SH File format
Plain text, one buffer per line.
The current buffer is prefixed with \f[CR]*\f[R], others with
\f[CR]\f[R].
Buffers without a filename (scratch, \f[CR][No Name]\f[R]) are skipped
on save.
.IP
.EX
* /home/me/project/src/main.c
  /home/me/project/src/foo.c
  /home/me/project/Makefile
.EE
.PP
Easy to edit by hand, easy to grep.
.SH Auto\-restore after \f[CR]:reload\f[R]
The \f[CR]reload\f[R] plugin sets \f[CR]HED_RELOAD=1\f[R] and writes the
session file just before \f[CR]execl\f[R]\-ing the new binary.
On startup, this plugin checks the env var via the
\f[CR]HOOK_STARTUP_DONE\f[R] hook, restores the buffers, deletes the
file, and unsets the env var.
No manual step needed.
.SH Underlying API
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\[dq]session/session.h\[dq]\f[R]

EdError session_save(const char *path);
EdError session_restore(const char *path);
.EE
.PP
Pure mechanic \[em] no policy.
Decides nothing about where to put the file, when to fire, or whether to
clean up.
Compose those concerns on top.
.SH Notes
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]session_restore\f[R] closes any empty unnamed placeholder buffer
that startup left behind, so the restored list isn\[cq]t padded with a
bogus \f[CR][No Name]\f[R] entry.
.IP \[bu] 2
The session file is overwritten on every save \[em] there\[cq]s no
multi\-session history yet.
If you want named sessions, copy the file out before saving.
